Add support for the Object Property Initialiser syntax.

Allows objects' properties to be set in shorter syntax.

Use is as follows:
Basic:
```
var x = {
  name: "OPI",
  type: "Syntax"
};
```
or:
```
var name = "OPI";
var x = {
  name,
  type: "Syntax"
};
```

A instance of an object may also prefix the initialiser:
```
class Person { ... }

var jack = Person() {
  name: "Jack",
  age: 27
}
```

I reviewed all the namespace references in all templates.

I noticed that we used 3 standards, listed below in order of frequency (most used -> least used)
- no namespace defined in templates
- namespace: {{ .Release.Namespace }}
- namespace: {{ .Values.namespace }}

I refactored all the templates with the second choice: namespace: {{ .Release.Namespace }}

It is a good standard and easy to manage without extra values.

